# Blazor Component CSS Handbook

## Purpose

This handbook defines the default CSS standard for one-file Blazor components used in R&D, dashboard, control-panel, and internal UI development.

The goal is not maximum abstraction. The goal is CSS that is:

* Local to the component
* Easy to read
* Easy to modify
* Hard to break accidentally
* Consistent across components
* Simple enough for rapid development
* Structured enough to be cleaned, reviewed, and reused

---

# 1. Component Boundary Rule

Every component must have one root CSS class.

```razor
<div class="component-name">
    ...
</div>
```

All component styles must be scoped under that root class.

```css
.component-name {
}

.component-name__element {
}

.component-name__element--modifier {
}
```

Do not style from generic selectors alone.

Avoid:

```css
button {
}

div > span {
}

.selected {
}
```

Prefer:

```css
.component-name__button {
}

.component-name__value {
}

.component-name__item--selected {
}
```

The root class is the component’s CSS boundary.

---

# 2. Naming Rule

Use role-based names, not appearance-based names.

Use this pattern:

```css
.component-name
.component-name__element
.component-name__element--state
.component-name__element--variant
```

Examples:

```css
.feed-rate-slider
.feed-rate-slider__label
.feed-rate-slider__track
.feed-rate-slider__value
.feed-rate-slider__button--disabled
```

Good names describe purpose:

```css
.dropdown__button
.dropdown__menu
.dropdown__item
.dropdown__item--selected
```

Bad names describe temporary appearance:

```css
.blue-box
.big-text
.left-panel
.round-thing
```

Appearance changes. Role usually remains stable.

---

# 3. Ownership Rule

A component controls its internal layout.

A parent controls external placement.

Therefore, component CSS should usually avoid external margins on the root.

Avoid:

```css
.component-name {
    margin-top: 24px;
}
```

Prefer:

```css
.component-name {
    width: 100%;
}
```

Use internal spacing inside the component:

```css
.component-name {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
}
```

The parent decides where the component sits. The component decides how its own contents are arranged.

---

# 4. CSS Ordering Rule

Properties inside each selector must follow this order:

```css
.selector {
    /* Layout */
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;

    /* Sizing */
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 0;
    height: auto;

    /* Box model */
    padding: 0.75rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--component-border);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    box-sizing: border-box;

    /* Visual */
    background: var(--component-bg);
    box-shadow: none;
    opacity: 1;

    /* Text */
    color: var(--component-text);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.4;
    text-align: left;

    /* Interaction */
    cursor: default;
    user-select: none;
    transition: background-color 120ms ease, border-color 120ms ease;
}
```

Not every selector needs every section.

But when properties exist, keep them in this order.

---

# 5. Layout Rule

Prefer modern layout tools.

Use:

```css
display: flex;
gap: 0.75rem;
align-items: center;
justify-content: space-between;
```

Or:

```css
display: grid;
grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto;
gap: 0.75rem;
```

Avoid positioning by accident.

Avoid:

```css
margin-left: 17px;
margin-top: 6px;
position: relative;
left: 12px;
top: -3px;
```

Use `position: absolute` only when the UI element is genuinely layered, floating, overlayed, or anchored.

Examples where positioning is acceptable:

```css
.dropdown__menu {
    position: absolute;
    top: 100%;
    left: 0;
}
```

```css
.tooltip {
    position: absolute;
}
```

Do not use positioning to fix poor layout structure.

---

# 6. Spacing Rule

Use `gap` for spacing between children.

Use `padding` for spacing inside a box.

Use `margin` only when the element genuinely needs spacing outside itself.

Preferred:

```css
.component-name {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
}
```

Preferred:

```css
.component-name__button {
    padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
}
```

Avoid:

```css
.component-name__item {
    margin-bottom: 12px;
}
```

Use consistent spacing values:

```css
0.25rem
0.5rem
0.75rem
1rem
1.5rem
2rem
```

Avoid random spacing values unless matching a specific design requirement.

---

# 7. Sizing Rule

Components should be fluid by default.

Use:

```css
width: 100%;
max-width: 100%;
min-width: 0;
box-sizing: border-box;
```

Use fixed sizes only when the component truly needs fixed dimensions.

Acceptable:

```css
.status-indicator {
    width: 0.75rem;
    height: 0.75rem;
}
```

Risky:

```css
.panel {
    width: 742px;
}
```

For flexible limits, prefer:

```css
width: min(100%, 40rem);
```

Or:

```css
font-size: clamp(0.875rem, 1vw, 1rem);
```

---

# 8. Variable Rule

Use CSS variables for repeated or configurable component values.

Place variables on the root class.

```css
.component-name {
    --component-bg: #1f1f1f;
    --component-border: #3a3a3a;
    --component-text: #ffffff;
    --component-accent: #4ea1ff;
    --component-radius: 0.5rem;
    --component-padding: 0.75rem;
}
```

Then consume them below:

```css
.component-name__button {
    padding: var(--component-padding);
    border-radius: var(--component-radius);
    background: var(--component-accent);
}
```

Use variables when a value is:

* Repeated
* Thematic
* Likely to change
* Shared across child elements
* Controlled by component parameters

Do not create variables for one-off values that are never reused.

---

# 9. State Rule

UI state should be represented through explicit state classes.

Preferred:

```razor
<button class="dropdown__item @(isSelected ? "dropdown__item--selected" : null)">
    @item.Label
</button>
```

```css
.dropdown__item--selected {
    background: var(--dropdown-selected-bg);
    font-weight: 600;
}
```

Common state modifiers:

```css
--selected
--active
--open
--closed
--disabled
--loading
--error
--warning
--success
--readonly
```

Avoid hiding important state inside complex selectors.

Avoid:

```css
.dropdown li:nth-child(3) span {
}
```

Prefer:

```css
.dropdown__item--selected {
}
```

State should be obvious from the markup and obvious from the CSS.

---

# 10. Interaction Rule

Interactive elements must define their normal, hover, focus, active, and disabled behavior when applicable.

Minimum standard:

```css
.component-name__button {
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background-color 120ms ease, border-color 120ms ease, color 120ms ease;
}

.component-name__button:hover {
    background: var(--button-hover-bg);
}

.component-name__button:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--component-accent);
    outline-offset: 2px;
}

.component-name__button:active {
    transform: translateY(1px);
}

.component-name__button:disabled,
.component-name__button--disabled {
    cursor: not-allowed;
    opacity: 0.5;
}
```

Never remove focus styling without replacing it.

Avoid:

```css
button:focus {
    outline: none;
}
```

Acceptable only if replaced:

```css
button:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--component-accent);
    outline-offset: 2px;
}
```

---

# 11. Specificity Rule

Keep selectors shallow.

Preferred:

```css
.component-name__item {
}
```

Acceptable:

```css
.component-name__item:hover {
}
```

Acceptable:

```css
.component-name__item--selected {
}
```

Avoid:

```css
.page .panel .component-name ul li button span {
}
```

Avoid:

```css
.component-name div div button:nth-child(2) {
}
```

Avoid `!important`.

If `!important` seems necessary, the CSS structure is probably wrong.

---

# 12. Element Selector Rule

Do not style raw elements globally inside a component unless scoped by the root class.

Avoid:

```css
button {
}
```

Acceptable:

```css
.component-name button {
}
```

Preferred:

```css
.component-name__button {
}
```

For maintainability, prefer class selectors over raw element selectors.

---

# 13. Typography Rule

Components should usually inherit the application font.

Avoid setting `font-family` inside every component.

Preferred:

```css
.component-name {
    color: var(--component-text);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
}
```

Use font sizes consistently:

```css
0.75rem
0.875rem
1rem
1.125rem
1.25rem
1.5rem
```

Use font weight intentionally:

```css
400 normal body text
500 emphasized UI text
600 labels, selected items, important values
700 headings or strong emphasis
```

Avoid using large font weights randomly.

---

# 14. Color Rule

Do not scatter repeated raw colors throughout the CSS.

Avoid:

```css
.card {
    background: #222;
}

.card__button {
    background: #222;
}

.card__value {
    color: #4ea1ff;
}
```

Prefer:

```css
.card {
    --card-bg: #222;
    --card-accent: #4ea1ff;
}

.card {
    background: var(--card-bg);
}

.card__button {
    background: var(--card-bg);
}

.card__value {
    color: var(--card-accent);
}
```

Use semantic variable names.

Good:

```css
--status-success
--status-warning
--status-error
--button-bg
--button-hover-bg
--panel-border
```

Bad:

```css
--green
--yellow
--red
--blue1
```

---

# 15. Border and Radius Rule

Use consistent border and radius values.

Recommended:

```css
border: 1px solid var(--component-border);
border-radius: 0.375rem;
border-radius: 0.5rem;
border-radius: 0.75rem;
```

Avoid random values:

```css
border-radius: 13px;
border-radius: 19px;
```

Use larger radius only when the design clearly calls for it.

---

# 16. Overflow Rule

Every component that displays dynamic content should handle overflow deliberately.

Common defaults:

```css
.component-name {
    min-width: 0;
    max-width: 100%;
}
```

For text truncation:

```css
.component-name__label {
    min-width: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    white-space: nowrap;
}
```

For scrollable content:

```css
.component-name__body {
    overflow: auto;
}
```

Do not allow accidental layout breakage from long labels, long values, large payloads, or dynamic data.

---

# 17. Responsive Rule

Prefer components that adapt to their container.

Use fluid layout first:

```css
.component-name {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
    gap: 0.75rem;
}
```

Use container queries when the component must change layout based on available space:

```css
.component-name {
    container-type: inline-size;
}

@container (max-width: 400px) {
    .component-name__row {
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: stretch;
    }
}
```

Use media queries only when the rule truly depends on viewport size.

---

# 18. Animation Rule

Animations should be small, fast, and purposeful.

Preferred properties:

```css
transform
opacity
background-color
border-color
color
```

Avoid animating expensive layout properties:

```css
width
height
top
left
margin
padding
```

Standard transition:

```css
transition: background-color 120ms ease, border-color 120ms ease, color 120ms ease;
```

Use longer animations only when the design specifically requires it.

Avoid decorative animation in industrial dashboards unless it improves clarity.

---

# 19. Razor Dynamic Styling Rule

Use dynamic classes for state.

Use CSS variables for dynamic values.

Preferred for state:

```razor
<div class="status-card @(IsActive ? "status-card--active" : "status-card--inactive")">
```

Preferred for values:

```razor
<div class="gauge" style="--gauge-value:@Value%;">
```

```css
.gauge__fill {
    width: var(--gauge-value);
}
```

Avoid large inline style strings.

Avoid:

```razor
<div style="width:@Value%; background:@Color; border-radius:12px; padding:10px;">
```

Inline styles are acceptable for small dynamic values that CSS cannot know ahead of time.

---

# 20. Comment Rule

Use comments to divide CSS sections, not to explain obvious properties.

Good:

```css
/* Root */
.component-name {
}

/* Header */
.component-name__header {
}

/* States */
.component-name--disabled {
}
```

Avoid:

```css
/* Makes text white */
color: white;
```

Comments should improve navigation, not create noise.

---

# 21. Canonical Component CSS Structure

Use this structure for most components.

```css
/* Root */
.component-name {
    --component-bg: #1f1f1f;
    --component-border: #3a3a3a;
    --component-text: #ffffff;
    --component-muted-text: #b5b5b5;
    --component-accent: #4ea1ff;
    --component-radius: 0.5rem;
    --component-padding: 0.75rem;

    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;

    width: 100%;
    min-width: 0;
    max-width: 100%;
    padding: var(--component-padding);
    border: 1px solid var(--component-border);
    border-radius: var(--component-radius);
    box-sizing: border-box;

    background: var(--component-bg);
    color: var(--component-text);
}

/* Header */
.component-name__header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.75rem;

    min-width: 0;
}

/* Title */
.component-name__title {
    min-width: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    white-space: nowrap;

    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.3;
}

/* Body */
.component-name__body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;

    min-width: 0;
}

/* Row */
.component-name__row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.75rem;

    min-width: 0;
}

/* Label */
.component-name__label {
    min-width: 0;

    color: var(--component-muted-text);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
}

/* Value */
.component-name__value {
    min-width: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    white-space: nowrap;

    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.4;
}

/* Button */
.component-name__button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.375rem;

    min-width: 0;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--component-border);
    border-radius: 0.375rem;
    box-sizing: border-box;

    background: transparent;
    color: var(--component-text);
    font: inherit;

    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background-color 120ms ease, border-color 120ms ease, color 120ms ease;
}

.component-name__button:hover {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
}

.component-name__button:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--component-accent);
    outline-offset: 2px;
}

.component-name__button:active {
    transform: translateY(1px);
}

.component-name__button:disabled,
.component-name__button--disabled {
    cursor: not-allowed;
    opacity: 0.5;
}

/* States */
.component-name--active {
    border-color: var(--component-accent);
}

.component-name--disabled {
    opacity: 0.6;
    pointer-events: none;
}
